{
  "format": "rg.carimport/1",
  "note": "One entry per imported car: source GLB in data/models/downloaded/, output id (data/models/imported/<id>/<id>.glb + .rig.json). forward/up: source-world axes when the automatic guess must be overridden. brake_parts: regex on node paths of parts that steer with the wheel but do not spin (calipers); they go under steer_<corner> (front) or susp_<corner> (rear) and are not part of the wheel. vehicle: the game vehicle file written from `base` with the model's wheel positions and the given tyre (one spec, or front/rear). materials: regexes on source material names renamed to paint / rim for the garage and drive colours (paint_tint_texture: a white-body copy of an atlas paint map, the paint keeps that map and paint_tint_factor as its colour, named paint_tinted). lights.rules: lamp triangles by node path / material regex and an ISO box (x, y, z [min, max] m, output frame, triangle centroid), first rule wins; kind indicator splits left/right by side; lights.required: kinds the check insists on. driver_eye: {at: ISO point} or {steering: node regex, offset: from the steering wheel's bbox centre}. light_look: emission colour and strength per lamp kind (the numbers of the cargen cars).",
